Z||000012||Indiana_resto_guy||08-07-2001||12:23 AM||||OK, it sounds like the distributor was dropped back in alright. Did you also reference the base plate of it to get to it's position as well? If not, just try turning it (the distributor)a bit to see if it starts. OR (best way) disconnect the coil wire, remove distributor cap, rotate engine by hand till the widest timing mark comes up to 10 degrees BTC with the rotor coming to #1 plug wire position (make note which wire is #1 before removing cap). Place cap on and rotate base plate to the #1 position and snug down the dis. retaining bolt, double check rotor position and reinstall cap and connect coil wire. It should now start if everything else is connected.||||reg||1
